{{- /* overlap: two normal-flow text blocks nudged onto the same region with a
       transform, so they visually collide without going through
       position:absolute — triggers `overlap`, and proves the rule still
       catches a collision that is not the badge/phase-pill kind of chrome. */ -}}
<p class="overlap-a">First label sits here.</p>
<p class="overlap-b">Second label lands on top of it.</p>
